# TypeScript hygiene (target state)

Broader language/React patterns: see `typescript-best-practices.mdc`.

## Types

- `strict` is on - do not weaken it
- No new `any` / `as any` escapes; type API responses with `src/types/*` aligned to backend schemas
- Prefer `Role` enum members over raw role strings in app code (tests/e2e may use enum values)
- Status strings that mirror backend (`complete` vs `completed`) must match `round_enums` / backend docs

## Imports

- Prefer the `@/` alias for new files and when rewriting imports (tests already do)
- Avoid deep `../../../../` chains when adding modules under `features/`

## Console & logging

- Production UI: no `console.log` / `console.error` litter - use `devLog`/`devError` or error UI
- `src/api/**` is hard no-console (CI)

## Dependencies

- Do not add Formik, Yup, or MUI Data Grid for new work
- Prefer deleting unused deps over wiring them "because they are installed"
- Long-term: OpenAPI codegen is welcome; until then keep `src/types` updated when schemas change in the same PR when feasible
